From: "adnan.drina" <adnan.drina@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:42:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] fix(guardrails): halt a cycle of redundant reads and
 identical pre-execution refusals

Two local additions (RHOAI3 V16-7, V16-9).

Read cycle. Every read-only call (a terminal read-only pipeline or an
idempotent read tool) is checked for new output: a line no read has
shown since the last evidence-changing call. A new read clears the
history. Reads that show nothing new are kept by exact identity (tool,
workdir, canonical arguments; nothing is normalised). When the trailing
3*L of them are exactly L distinct calls (2 <= L <= 32), each made 3
times in any order, the turn halts with read_cycle_no_new_content_halt,
naming the cycle. An evidence-changing call (write, patch, code
execution, a non-read-only command) starts a new phase. A single
repeated call stays with the identical-call guard. The read-only
parser now accepts quoted patterns that contain operator characters.

Refusals. A call refused before execution (a pre_tool_call hook or a
scope denial) never reached the guardrails. It now counts as a failed
call of that tool (exact-failure and same-tool-failure families), and
the 3rd consecutive refusal of the identical call with the identical
refusal text halts with identical_refusal_halt, naming the tool and the
refusal. Executed calls keep their thresholds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
